### What the page covers

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| **Purpose** | Tab order must match visual reading order; documents all four violation kinds from the check module (`positive-tabindex`, `reverse-vertical`, `reverse-horizontal`, `handbook-chrome-tab-suppressed`) with thresholds (72px / 96px / 40px / 16 links / 48 tab stops). |
| **Passing signals** | Natural tab flow through `site-header` → **Kpn** / `landing-nav` → `main#main` → **Ksf**; no positive tabindex; dropdown panels in DOM order. |
| **Failing signals** | Positive tabindex, vertical jumps, `flex-row-reverse` on **Kpn**, excessive `tabindex="-1"` on sidebar/ToC chrome. |
| **Before example** | **Kpn** with `flex-row-reverse` (horizontal inversion) + hero CTA with `tabindex="3"`. |
| **After example** | Skip link + **Kpn** LTR DOM order + `fs-nav-dropdown` + footer **Ksf**; no tabindex overrides. |
| **Evidence & remediation** | `navFocusOrderReport` fields, six-step remediation, harness/test commands. |
| **Related rules** | `DET.LANDMARKS.REQUIRED`, `DET.NAV.DEPTH`, `DET.NAV.DEDUP`, `DET.NAV.BREADCRUMB`, `DET.NAV.IN_PAGE_TOC`, `DET.APP.FOCUS_TRAP`. |

